{"name":"Bloodline","hex":"#882200","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"bloodline","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The abstract link between a person and their ancestors.","The pedigree of an animal."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bloodline"}],"entries":[{"title":"Bloodline (TV series)","blocks":[{"text":"Bloodline is an American psychological thriller television series created by Todd A. Kessler, Glenn Kessler, and Daniel Zelman, and produced by Sony Pictures Television. The series premiered on February 9, 2015, in the Berlinale Special Galas section of the 65th Berlin International Film Festival, and the 13-episode first season premiered in its entirety, on Netflix, on March 20, 2015. On March 31, 2015, Bloodline was renewed for a 10-episode second season that debuted on May 27, 2016. On July 13, 2016, Netflix renewed Bloodline for a 10-episode third season, later confirmed to be the final season. The third and final season was released on May 26, 2017."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/9/93/Bloodline_TV_Series_Poster.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bloodline_(TV_series)","wikidata":"Q18643684"},{"title":"Bloodline (1979 film)","blocks":[{"text":"Bloodline is a 1979 thriller film directed by Terence Young and starring Audrey Hepburn, Ben Gazzara, James Mason, Claudia Mori, Irene Papas, Michelle Phillips, Maurice Ronet, and Romy Schneider. Adapted by Laird Koenig from the 1977 novel of the same name by Sidney Sheldon, it follows international pharmaceutical heiress Elizabeth Roffe who is targeted for death by unknown members of her extended family, while a serial killer simultaneously crisscrosses Europe, murdering women in snuff films. It was the only R-rated film ever made by Hepburn. Bloodline was the second film Hepburn made after coming back from an eight-year retirement from acting. Despite this, it was her first film in three years since her comeback role in Robin And Marian (1976)."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/8/8e/Bloodlineposter.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bloodline_(1979_film)","wikidata":"Q1768311"},{"title":"Heredity","blocks":[{"text":"Heredity, also called inheritance or biological inheritance, is the passing on of genetic information from parents to their offspring. It may occur through sexual or asexual reproduction, where new cells are produced from either individual cells underdoing cell division or two cells combining genomes, respectively. Through heredity, genetic variations in populations can accumulate and cause species to evolve by natural selection. The study of heredity in biology is genetics."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f0/Hybridogenesis_in_water_frogs_gametes.svg/330px-Hybridogenesis_in_water_frogs_gametes.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Heredity","wikidata":"Q178694"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/66/Jug_Ear_Heredity.jpg/500px-Jug_Ear_Heredity.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/66/Jug_Ear_Heredity.jpg/500px-Jug_Ear_Heredity.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Heredity of phenotypic traits: a father and son with prominent ears and crowns","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AJug_Ear_Heredity.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/0/0c/DNA_animation.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 1x","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/0/0c/DNA_animation.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","alt":"DNA structure. Bases are in the centre, surrounded by phosphate–sugar chains in a double helix.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ADNA_animation.gif"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/52/Aristotle%27s_model_of_Inheritance.png/500px-Aristotle%27s_model_of_Inheritance.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/52/Aristotle%27s_model_of_Inheritance.png/500px-Aristotle%27s_model_of_Inheritance.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Aristotle's model of inheritance. The heat/cold part is largely symmetrical, though influenced on the father's side by other factors, but the form part is not.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAristotle's_model_of_Inheritance.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/21/Autosomal_dominant.png/500px-Autosomal_dominant.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/21/Autosomal_dominant.png/500px-Autosomal_dominant.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"An example pedigree chart of an autosomal dominant disorder","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAutosomal_dominant.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5d/Autosomal_recessive.png/500px-Autosomal_recessive.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5d/Autosomal_recessive.png/500px-Autosomal_recessive.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"An example pedigree chart of an autosomal recessive disorder","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAutosomal_recessive.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ac/Sex_linked_inheri